  "source_review": {
    "review": [
      "One fixed11-label unchanged RAM program reads each actual header cell, resets a natural decoding counter, and uses castNat/equalReal/increment to decode it. mulNat accumulates the product; the program performs no memory writes and uses no real-to-natural or header oracle opcode.",
      "The explicit headerDecoderEmbedding is an actual finite instruction/register embedding of the already verified decoder. Ordinary-iteration helpers preserve its literal state relation and outside-frame registers. Those helpers concern ordinaryStep; the subsequent legal-trace contract uses the proved scalar nature of this program.",
      "For every natural header count and every memory whose first count cells are the stated natural casts, every legal trace from actual initial returns the exact prefix product with unchanged memory. The time is the proved sum(3*value+7)+4 and actual CostThrough is bounded by that time. Count0 and zero header values are included.",
      "The caller contract at arbitrary trace offset returns running at mapped local halt10 before executing that label, retains the exact product/state relation, and bounds actual caller charges by its prefix plus sum(3*value+7)+3."
    ],
    "limits": "Initialization component only. It assumes natural-valued input cells, supplied separately by the immutable original InputMemory bridge. The complete approximation program and total cost are not inferred."
  },
